meta {
  name: Update a comment
  type: http
  seq: 49
}

patch {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/comments/:id
  body: json
  auth: none
}

params:query {
  seed: 1
  ~locale: 
  ~conflict: 
  ~delay: 
  ~trickle: 
  ~status: 
  ~fail: 
  ~auth: 
}

params:path {
  id: 1
}

body:json {
  {
    "postId": 7204,
    "userId": 3024,
    "name": "Felipa Lind",
    "email": "Marcos80@example.net",
    "body": "ST52aS6qX"
  }
}

docs {
  Validates the fields sent and answers with the comment merged with them, with `updatedAt` set.

  `postId` must name a record in `/posts`, and `userId` must name a record in `/users` at the same `seed` and `locale`, or the write answers `422`.

  By default nothing is stored, so a later read returns the same data as before and the response is what the write would have produced. With the session on (`--session`, `REST_IN_PIECES_SESSION=true` or `createApp({ session: true })`), the change is kept in memory and later reads at the same `seed` and `locale` see it, until `POST /reset`. A session that is full answers `507`.
}
